# Corpus and derived data are bytes, not source. Git must not translate line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on at least one machine in play, which stored these blobs
# as LF and expanded them to CRLF on checkout. That silently broke source_sha256: the
# nine Internet Archive OCR scans were fetched and hashed as LF, so every Windows
# checkout produced files whose bytes no longer matched the sha256 their manifest
# attests. On Linux the failure inverts and the 72 Gutenberg files break instead, so
# before this file NO checkout of this repository could verify all 81.
#
# The corpus is genuinely mixed-newline: Project Gutenberg serves CRLF, the Archive.org
# scans are LF, and each manifest records the file as it was actually downloaded.
# Preserving the bytes is what keeps the manifest true.
data/raw/**/*.txt     -text
data/raw/**/*.json    -text
data/clean/**/*.jsonl -text
